JR is convenient if you want to travel throughout the country.
The JR transport network serves the whole country.
Besides slightly more spacious Green Cars, compartments for small groups and individuals are available.
It's not cheap, but it's convenient.
JR has a nationwide network of old, narrow gauge train service in addition to its newer, standard gauge train service.
The old network has local, semi express, express and limited express trains.
There also are limited express night trains with sleeping accommodations, which go very far.
JR's train services and subways are conveniently networked.
During morning and evening rush hours, trains run every two or three minutes.
The fare is not a flat fare. The fare varies according to the distance.
In most cases we buy a ticket from a vending machine.
There is no first or second class in the urban trains.
Fares to destination are shown on a panel at each station.
But, the station names are mostly written in Japanese only. So, it may be difficult to understand.
If you don't know how much it is just buy the cheaper ticket and pay the difference as you go out of your station.
Almost all the station gates are automatic.
In that case you go through the manned gate.
For the adjustment of underpaid fare, too, more and more automatic machines are being installed.
When you insert your ticket into the slot, the additional amount is shown. Then, you pay the amount and get an adjustment ticket.
You can ask a conductor on the train for the fare adjustment. He comes around now and then.
Be sure to keep your ticket until you arrive at your station. You can't go through the gate without it.
To travel to the suburbs, you can use many private lines besides JR.
On the suburban lines, there are various types of trains such as local, express, rapid and special express.
To see whether or not a train stops at your station, you should check the board or ask a station clerk.
You don't have to pay any extra charge for the express trains to the suburbs.
But, extra payment is required for the limited express trains with seat reservation which go to popular tourist resorts.
An announcement of the next stop is made on every train without exception.
