I'll call the number and find it for you.
I found it.
Here it is. Two thousand and sixty yen, please.
Thank you. Can I have a receipt, please?
Mister, you left your envelope behind.
Airway networks in Japan are well developed.
There are roughly sixty airports which have regular flight services.
Can I make a reservation on a plane?
Certainly. Which flight?
Yes, I have an open ticket.
May I see your ticket?
You can get ANA flight fifty-nine, which leaves Tokyo at nine fifty-five and arrives at Sapporo at eleven twenty-five.
What time do the next flights leave?
There are JAL and ANA flights which leave at ten fifty-five. But, unfortunately both flights are full.
You are booked. Here is your ticket.
I put a "reserved" sticker on your ticket.
Please check in twenty minutes before departure.
Domestic flights leave from Haneda Airport.
It takes about forty minutes by a rapid train.
It will take about one hour and ten minutes by bus.
Thank you very much. Have a pleasant trip.
Now that deluxe boats are available, the Tokyo Bay cruise is popular among young people.
Sightseeing boats are available on most large lakes.
There are boats modeled after a pirate ship or an old paddle-wheel steamer. Some others look like a swan or a whale.
